app: build sections are not built for compose stacks; give the service an image
app: port 80 is published on the host as 8080; instead add a domain for container port 80, or open it on IP:port from the service's networking
app: UDP port 53 is not supported
app: bind mount ./data:/data is not supported; use a named volume (files outside the stack are not on the node)
app: env_file is not read; put those variables in the stack's environment
app: deploy mode global is not supported; choose nodes and replicas in the service's settings
app: placement constraints are ignored; choose nodes in the service's settings
app: logging driver syslog is ignored; logs are kept on the node
proxy: network_mode host is not supported; the service joins the stack's private network
proxy: privileged mode is not supported and is ignored
proxy: cap_add (NET_ADMIN) is ignored
proxy: mounting the Docker socket gives full control of the node and is not supported
proxy: container_name is ignored; containers get their own names
proxy: restart always is replaced by the service's crash policy
proxy: Traefik labels are ignored; add domains to the service instead
debug: skipped, its profile is not active
network back: custom networks are replaced by the stack's private network
volume shared: external volumes are not supported; a new empty volume is created
secret token: reading ./token.txt from a file is not supported; use content or environment
variable MISSING_KEY is not set; it was replaced with an empty value
